      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a line-for-line copy of ClientHttp2Session.addChannelHandler() apart from the log strings and streamId() vs id(), which makes three protocol variants of the same handler. It also re-states an unwritten rule: SimpleChannelInboundHandler releases the response once channelRead0 returns, so the FullHttpResponse passed to onSuccess is only valid during that call. Could we pull the handler into a shared class, and document the lifetime rule on ClientSession.invoke()?",
